The spectra are of **D, pentan-2-one**.

**¹H NMR:** four environments (pentanoic acid would have five, including a COOH signal near 9–13 ppm, which is absent):
- singlet (3H) near 1.9 ppm: $\text{CH}_3$ next to C=O, no neighbouring H;
- triplet (2H) near 2.2 ppm: $\text{CH}_2$ next to C=O, split by 2 H;
- sextet (2H) near 1.35 ppm: middle $\text{CH}_2$, 5 neighbouring H;
- triplet (3H) near 0.7 ppm: terminal $\text{CH}_3$.

**IR:** strong sharp C=O absorption near 1720 cm⁻¹, C–H near 2850–3000 cm⁻¹, and **no** very broad O–H absorption (2500–3300 cm⁻¹) that an acid would show.

**Mass spectrum:** molecular ion $m/z$ 86 $= M(\text{C}_5\text{H}_{10}\text{O})$ (the acid would be 102). Base peak 43 is $[\text{CH}_3\text{CO}]^+$ (and/or $[\text{C}_3\text{H}_7]^+$); 71 is loss of $\text{CH}_3$.
